  "body": "Stacked on #4469 - do not merge before #4469.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe generic component editor redraws a holder after a gauge length edit. It found the built-in holder by `library_ref`, id or name (`holder_entry`), and drew that holder's outline at the new length. A user holder with a library name and a wider body under the flange envelope then got the library body. That body is thinner than the real steel, and the outline goes into the collision checks.\n\n- New `ComponentGeometry::regauged_holder` (`crates/tools/src/component_geometry_regauge.rs`). It gives the built-in outline at the new gauge length only when both conditions are true:\n  - The holder's outline is the built-in holder's outline at the holder's own gauge length.\n  - The new outline is the old outline with one straight cylindrical section made longer or shorter. The nose keeps its shape from the nose face, the flange keeps its shape from the gauge line, and the section keeps its old radius.\n- Each other case is refused by name, and nothing changes:\n  - `NotLibrary`: a library name on another outline.\n  - `NoSection`: the outline shows no body section. This is a shrink chuck whose body the flange envelope covers, and also its look-alike with a wider hidden body. The two outlines are the same, so both are refused.\n- `component_edit::build` uses the new function. The edit stays one undoable `EditDocumentComponent`.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/4496-generic-editor-gauge.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-ui` lib: `egui_app::tests::tool_library_generic_gauge::a_gauge_edit_never_draws_the_library_body_over_wider_steel` - the look-alike edit is refused by name, it is no undo step, and the outline stays the same. An ER20 chuck copy still takes the edit as one undo step, and undo restores it. This test is red on the parent head `1e899ad` (\"a refused edit is no undo step\", left 8): log `gate-4496-1e899ad-before.log`.\n- `camcraft-tools` lib, `component_geometry::regauge::tests`:\n  - `a_look_alike_with_a_wider_hidden_body_is_refused_by_name` - also shows the defect: the library body at the new length is smaller than the Ø50 steel.\n  - `a_wider_visible_body_under_a_library_name_is_refused_by_name`\n  - `each_library_holder_that_shows_its_body_edits_as_before` - each library entry: a longer gauge length gives the library outline, never smaller than the old outline at any height below the gauge line; a shorter one inside the body section gives it back. Only covered shrink chucks are refused.\n  - `a_holder_without_a_port_or_a_body_is_refused`\n\n## Gate (head `3d9ca49`, one lanes run, `--needs app`, log `gate-4496-3d9ca49.log`)\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 182 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. The base is `origin/main`, so the plan also covers the diff of #4469.\n- Pinning tests: `component_geometry::regauge` 4 passed; `tool_library_generic_gauge` 1 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- Heavy: `cargo xtask gate heavy --dry-run --base origin/main` reaches the `app` and `motion` heavy lanes only through the `camcraft-tools` dependency. 0 heavy tests exist for the changed code: no `#[ignore]` test calls `regauged_holder` or `component_edit::build`. So no targeted heavy step ran. The pinning tests above are the targeted tests, and they are not heavy.\n- Example catalog suites: no post or toolpath changed. The quick plan ran `example_catalog` and it passed.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe generic component editor, a user holder \"BT40 Shrink 20 mm\" with a Ø50 body under the flange envelope, gauge length 90 -> 110 mm, then Apply component.\n\nBefore (parent `1e899ad`): the edit lands without a message, and the library body at 110 mm is thinner than the steel.\n\n![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4501/before.png)\n\nAfter: the edit is refused by name, and the holder does not change.\n\n![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4501/after.png)\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A user holder with arcs in its outline. It is refused (`NotLibrary`), because the library outlines have no arcs.\n- A covered shrink chuck copy can no longer take a gauge length edit in the generic editor. The user picks the built-in holder again at the new length, or edits the outline. #4455 has the same limit for the holder form.\n- No change to toolpaths, posts or the project file format.\n\nUI `#[test]` count: 2010 before, 2011 after. `camcraft-tools`: 286 before, 290 after.\n\nChangelog: The generic component editor refuses a holder gauge length edit by name when the holder's outline does not show the body that the edit makes longer or shorter; it never draws the library body over wider steel.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #4496\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
